Return awk's mktime() result as a time_t rather than an int.
do_mktime() passed mktime()'s result through an int, so with a 64-bit
time_t any time after 03:14:07 UTC on 19 January 2038 wrapped around to
a negative number.

---
 editors/awk.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/editors/awk.c
+++ b/editors/awk.c
@@ -2989,7 +2989,7 @@
 	return match_no;
 }
 
-static NOINLINE int do_mktime(const char *ds)
+static NOINLINE time_t do_mktime(const char *ds)
 {
 	struct tm then;
 	int count;
